cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This metadata is INCOMPLETE. It contains only fields that could be verified
  from the local repository itself. Author affiliations, ORCID identifiers,
  funding and publication metadata are deliberately absent rather than guessed. See docs/LOCAL_RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md before citing or releasing.
title: >-
  Boundary-aware spectral propagation for 1D quantum dynamics
abstract: >-
  Companion code for a study of how the spectral transform used inside a
  split-operator step determines the boundary topology represented by the
  numerical scheme and by its quantum-circuit realisation. Includes a validated
  quantum sine transform circuit, a direct periodic-versus-Dirichlet comparison
  against an independent reference, a tilted-well Trotter benchmark under
  Dirichlet boundaries, and logical resource estimates reported with their
  assumptions.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT

